— asset-pipeline agent, on behalf of KirkDiggler","path":"rulebooks/dnd5e/encounter/data.go","line":null,"originalLine":63,"url":"https://github.com/KirkDiggler/rpg-toolkit/pull/924#discussion_r3760458023","createdAt":"2026-08-11T18:00:07Z"}]}},{"isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"comments":{"nodes":[{"author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"body":"ConnectionData's FromPosition/ToPosition are required value fields. When loading pre-v0.2 encounter JSON (where these fields didn't exist), json.Unmarshal will set them to the zero position (0,0) with no way to distinguish “missing endpoints” from a legitimate endpoint at (0,0). That can silently change topology/behavior on load instead of rejecting or migrating old data.","path":"rulebooks/dnd5e/encounter/data.go","line":96,"originalLine":87,"url":"https://github.com/KirkDiggler/rpg-toolkit/pull/924#discussion_r3760175718","createdAt":"2026-08-11T17:20:06Z"},{"author":{"login":"KirkDiggler"},"body":"Verified and fixed in 095e6f5 — this was a real silent-topology hazard: a missing endpoint unmarshaled to (0,0), which is a legal cell, so old/hand-authored blobs would have gained invented topology instead of a rejection (and the design's "v0.1 blobs that declared connections fail v0.2 load" claim wasn't actually enforced). Endpoints are now `*PositionData` with presence required at load: nil → `ErrInvalidData` + `ErrBadConnection` with a discriminating "missing from_position"/"missing to_position" message. Both new one-defect rejection rows are mutant-verified. Wire shape of present endpoints is unchanged; `ToData` always populates both.

